# Security headers for every static asset.
#
# This file rather than the Worker, because a request for a path that matches
# an asset never reaches the Worker at all: with `assets.binding` set and
# `run_worker_first` unset, Cloudflare's asset server answers first and the
# script is only invoked on a miss. So `worker/index.ts` sets the same headers
# on the SPA fallback it serves for an unmatched path, and this covers
# everything else. The two lists must agree — change one, change the other.
#
# The CSP is deliberately partial, and the reasoning lives beside the copy in
# `worker/index.ts`: `frame-ancestors`, `object-src` and `base-uri` are free on
# a one-origin page that frames nothing, while `script-src` and `connect-src`
# need a nonce for the inline SW registration in `Base.astro` and a decision
# about `lib/feeds.ts`'s direct-fetch fallback. Half of it is worth more than
# none of it; the other half is a build change, not a header.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
